[36m(TaskRunner pid=490033)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=490033)[0m ### Step 1: Understand the problem
[36m(TaskRunner pid=490033)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=490033)[0m We are dealing with numbers in base $ b $, where the digits must satisfy $ 0 \leq $ digit $ < b $. Since the digits are 7 and 9 (in the numbers $ 17_b $ and $ 97_b $), this implies that $ b > 9 $, as the digit 9 is used.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=490033)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=490033)[0m We are to find all such bases $ b > 9 $ where $ 17_b $ divides $ 97_b $, and then sum them up.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=490033)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=490033)[0m ---
[36m(TaskRunner pid=490033)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=490033)[0m ### Step 2: Convert the numbers from base $ b $ to base 10
[36m(TaskRunner pid=490033)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=490033)[0m Recall:  
[36m(TaskRunner pid=490033)[0m - $ 17_b = 1 \cdot b + 7 = b + 7 $
[36m(TaskRunner pid=490033)[0m - $ 97_b = 9 \cdot b + 7 = 9b + 7 $
[36m(TaskRunner pid=490033)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=490033)[0m We are looking for all integers $ b > 9 $ such that:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=490033)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=490033)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=490033)[0m b + 7 \mid 9b + 7
[36m(TaskRunner pid=490033)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=490033)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=490033)[0m That is, $ b + 7 $ divides $ 9b + 7 $.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=490033)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=490033)[0m ---
[36m(TaskRunner pid=490033)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=490033)[0m ### Step 3: Use the divisibility condition
[36m(TaskRunner pid=490033)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=490033)[0m Let $ d = b + 7 $, so we want $ d \mid 9b + 7 $. Since $ d = b + 7 $, we can write:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=490033)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=490033)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=490033)[0m b = d - 7
[36m(TaskRunner pid=490033)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=490033)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=490033)[0m Now substitute into $ 9b + 7 $:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=490033)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=490033)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=490033)[0m 9b + 7 = 9(d - 7) + 7 = 9d - 63 + 7 = 9d - 56
[36m(TaskRunner pid=490033)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=490033)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=490033)[0m We are to find when $ d \mid 9d - 56 $, which is equivalent to:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=490033)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=490033)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=490033)[0m d \mid (9d - 56) - 9d = -56
[36m(TaskRunner pid=490033)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=490033)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=490033)[0m So we have:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=490033)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=490033)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=490033)[0m d \mid -56 \Rightarrow d \mid 56
[36m(TaskRunner pid=490033)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=490033)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=490033)[0m So $ d = b + 7 $ must be a **positive divisor of 56**, and also $ b > 9 \Rightarrow d > 16 $.
